prompts.prompt:
The first two provided images are approved food atlases from the same game. Use them ONLY as the style reference: match their hand-painted gouache and coloured-pencil rendering, their slightly top-down three-quarter view, their warm palette, their lighting, their level of detail and their clean edges. Do NOT copy any of their subjects. The third provided image is the current pickle atlas. Its top-left icon, the pickle barrel, has a problem of scale: the barrel holds only two cucumbers, and they look one metre long.

Create ONE landscape bitmap atlas, 2:1, a precisely regular grid of 4 columns by 2 rows of equal square cells. Only ONE cell holds an icon: cell 1, the top-left cell. The other seven cells stay completely empty and fully transparent, with nothing in them at all.

Cell 1. PICKLE BARREL (the source of the pickle chain): a squat, old, wide wooden barrel of dark oak staves bound with three black iron hoops, seen from slightly above so its open top is clearly visible. The barrel is about knee-high, so everything inside it is small next to it. It is FULL to the top with cloudy pale brine and a crowded mix of DIFFERENT PICKLES, all at their true small size:
- two whole round heads of pale yellow-green sour cabbage, the largest things inside;
- several small, finger-sized dark-green gherkins;
- a few small round green tomatoes;
- one or two small red peppers;
- sprigs of dill and a piece of horseradish root.
A round wooden lid leans against the side of the barrel, with a smooth river stone on the ground beside it. Keep the icon the same size in its cell as the current top-left icon.

Edges: hard, clean, cut-out edges, like the style reference. No glow, no halo, no rim light, no haze, no vignette, no soft fringe. No steam, no splashes, no drips in the air, no sparkles, no floating particles. The background is truly TRANSPARENT everywhere: alpha zero right up to the edge of the icon and in all the other cells. No backdrop, no grey panels, no checkerboard, no coloured matte, no grid lines, no frames, no cast shadow on a floor.

Layout rules: the icon fits inside the central 72% width and 72% height of its cell, with a fully transparent margin on all four sides. Nothing crosses into a neighbouring cell. No text, numbers, letters, labels or logos anywhere. One 2:1 landscape image, high resolution, crisp silhouette, true alpha transparency.
